      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i moved away from the lab after that accident in sector 4 but i cant stop seeing these things. it's like my vision is overlaid with these shifting color densities... like i saw a massive red pulse over a gas station earlier and i swear i could feel the tension in the air right before a truck nearly clipped the pump. then i see these tiny blue sparks during stuff that's just... random. i've been reading about quantum decoherence and i was wondering if it's possible my exposure actually tuned my neural pathways to perceive probability amplitudes as color frequencies? like is there a theoretical way the particle stream could have turned my visual cortex into a sort of live probability map?",
